# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. A tree added back after a decommission takes no
# boundary on its sibling, so its fence lifts on the fresh bootstrap before the
# peer has applied the sibling's records written before the re-add. The origin
# purged the sub-saga while the tree was removed, so the import carries bare
# committed rows while the sibling's terminal is still outstanding.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingFreshReaddNoBoundary
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a tree added back to the peer takes no boundary on its sibling
PERTURBS: ReaddFresh
BOUNDS: LossPath = 4, JoinStart = 0, SagaOutcome = 0, Shape = 1, PreHold = 0, DialFaults = 0

--- FIND
    /\ ubnd' = ubnd \cup {r \in outbox : ~Aff(r)}
    /\ bcaught' = FALSE

--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no boundary at the re-add.
    /\ ubnd' = ubnd
    /\ bcaught' = FALSE

--- END
